#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157868 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157316 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "32cd0921-2ed0-5b05-985a-e1849e98da10" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Probability of a Geometric Random Variable on a Bounded Interval"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "986ab300-81b2-59eb-a0cd-62ba8d6c153b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.035" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186156130} {:answer/id #uuid "e87d6839-b3dc-5320-bed5-098444affde1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.132" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186156131} {:answer/id #uuid "ed5c021d-8d89-5701-95fa-2b18fa234975" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.078" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186156132} {:answer/id #uuid "15a992f6-84bc-5672-9e51-80d812a13f47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.159" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186156133} {:answer/id #uuid "2b95dd55-35e9-5aca-a0cb-2370b157a2a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.097" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186156134}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ed5c021d-8d89-5701-95fa-2b18fa234975" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.078" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186156132} :answer-field/id #uuid "433b26e7-cbdf-5a51-bc6c-19eb63ac7ea2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186156129}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1c241a6a-1a9e-5d8e-adf5-2fd9b0826eb3" :question/math-academy-id "q-85277" :question/problem "At a water bottle factory, every batch of $1\\,000$ water bottles has $20$ water bottles (on average) on which the label is upside down. If an inspector comes to inspect the water bottles, what is the probability that they will find an upside down label before checking the $5$th bottle? Round your answer to $3$ decimal places." :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "A geometric random variable $X$ with probability of success $p$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=(1-p)^{x-1}p\n$$\n\nLet $X$ be the number of bottles checked until a defect is found. On average, the chance of finding an upside down label on any water bottle is \n\n$$\np=\\frac{20}{1\\,000}=0.02.\n$$\n\nSo, the number of bottles that the inspector checks before finding an upside down label can be modeled as a geometric random variable with a probability of success $p=0.02.$\n\nSo, $X∼\\text{Geom}(0.02).$ In this case, $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =(1-0.02)^{x-1}(0.02) \\\\  & =(0.98)^{x-1}(0.02)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the probability of finding an upside down label before checking the $5$th bottle is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<5) & =P(X\\in \\{1,2,3,4\\}) \\\\  & =f(1)+f(2)+f(3)+f(4) \\\\  & =(0.98)^{1-1}(0.02)+(0.98)^{2-1}(0.02)+(0.98)^{3-1}(0.02)+(0.98)^{4-1}(0.02) \\\\  & =(0.02)+(0.98)(0.02)+(0.98)^{2}(0.02)+(0.98)^{3}(0.02) \\\\  & =[1+0.98+(0.98)^{2}+(0.98)^{3}](0.02) \\\\  & ≈0.078\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186540080 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157315 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "88cf7c0e-8c1d-5a92-805f-0a81ee887546" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Probability of a Geometric Random Variable at a Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "38a40095-28ea-5b29-9f46-5d1722a2dc00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.095" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539584} {:answer/id #uuid "4ecdbb4d-cd29-5c6c-8d54-821afb7fd664" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.160" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539619} {:answer/id #uuid "511ee1e7-4a2e-5ac2-b693-bbdf3c003f14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.098" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539621} {:answer/id #uuid "bd14f852-afc2-5508-a508-f915bcd1125c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.112" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539806} {:answer/id #uuid "c19ac48b-f028-591b-b391-957b90b26cb8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.125" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539813}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c19ac48b-f028-591b-b391-957b90b26cb8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.125" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539813} :answer-field/id #uuid "02f2874f-c8cb-5424-9558-d25dbc1321ab" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539918}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "adc9ba22-54ae-50d6-b1c5-428a57977aea" :question/math-academy-id "q-85881" :question/problem "An experiment consists of tossing a fair coin until it comes up heads. What is the probability that we get our first head on the $3$rd toss? Round your answer to $3$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "A geometric random variable $X$ with probability of success $p$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=(1-p)^{x-1}p\n$$\n\nLet $X$ be the number of times the coin is tossed until it comes up heads. Since the chance of getting a head in every toss is $50%,$ the number of tosses until it comes up heads can be modeled as a geometric random variable with a probability of success\n\n$$\np=50%=\\frac{50}{100}=0.5.\n$$\n\nSo, $X∼\\text{Geom}(0.5).$ In this case, $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =(1-0.5)^{x-1}(0.5) \\\\  & =(0.5)^{x-1}(0.5)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the probability that head appears in the $3$rd toss is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=3) & =f(3) \\\\  & =(0.5)^{3-1}(0.5) \\\\  & =(0.5)^{2}(0.5) \\\\  & ≈0.125\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186540073 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157316 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "32cd0921-2ed0-5b05-985a-e1849e98da10" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Probability of a Geometric Random Variable on a Bounded Interval"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ed681c4-3034-59aa-a498-ea702cbb65c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.512" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539540} {:answer/id #uuid "2e6c7f4a-9255-55cc-ab48-64524d9d60bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.478" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539566} {:answer/id #uuid "2f594278-070e-5cca-b2b4-69634d02b41b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.391" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539568} {:answer/id #uuid "82348db0-740d-5037-8bfb-dd1638b0599c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.423" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539694} {:answer/id #uuid "bb376c02-f849-5a37-bcfc-6f47602f5bc8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.501" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539803}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2e6c7f4a-9255-55cc-ab48-64524d9d60bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.478" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539566} :answer-field/id #uuid "0d865ca2-a464-54ee-8571-e4cc8b40fa53" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539925}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "934447c8-2b56-5fbe-8d1c-94052a2dad02" :question/math-academy-id "q-85889" :question/problem "A lottery decides that $3$ out of every $20$ lottery tickets will win a special prize. If a player wants to win a special prize, what is the probability of finding a prize before purchasing their $5$th ticket? Round your answer to $3$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "A geometric random variable $X$ with probability of success $p$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=(1-p)^{x-1}p\n$$\n\nLet $X$ be the number of tickets purchased until a special prize is found. On average, the chance of finding a special prize on a single ticket is \n\n$$\np=\\frac{3}{20}=0.15.\n$$\n\nSo, the number of tickets that the player should purchase before they find a special prize can be modeled as a geometric random variable with a probability of success $p=0.15.$\n\nSo, $X∼\\text{Geom}(0.15).$ In this case, $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =(1-0.15)^{x-1}(0.15) \\\\  & =(0.85)^{x-1}(0.15)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the probability of finding a special prize before the $5$th ticket is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<5) & =P(X\\in \\{1,2,3,4\\}) \\\\  & =f(1)+f(2)+f(3)+f(4) \\\\  & =(0.85)^{1-1}(0.15)+(0.85)^{2-1}(0.15)+(0.85)^{3-1}(0.15)+(0.85)^{4-1}(0.15) \\\\  & =(0.15)+(0.85)(0.15)+(0.85)^{2}(0.15)+(0.85)^{3}(0.15) \\\\  & =[1+0.85+(0.85)^{2}+(0.85)^{3}](0.15) \\\\  & ≈0.478\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186540104 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157317 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "42f47d95-9f20-5488-98c4-cb80278a7cf3" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Probability of a Geometric Random Variable on an Unbounded Interval"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11d7504b-2828-5ed4-ab73-97d26b31abe0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.34" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539513} {:answer/id #uuid "79e93ad4-10ea-55a5-b833-af0a652dd041" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.62" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539683} {:answer/id #uuid "923cac8c-34f5-5ea2-bb76-7bdba561dd9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.49" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539721} {:answer/id #uuid "ab51231a-c4b2-5897-b2e4-e89b02c56f79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.38" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539768} {:answer/id #uuid "b141e339-58d5-542d-a915-4a9424c25f13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.59" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539780}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "923cac8c-34f5-5ea2-bb76-7bdba561dd9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.49" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539721} :answer-field/id #uuid "e64d04fb-cb14-517f-be04-f2bf97158deb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540005}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e49d61e7-549c-5568-9bc1-1e99e4e1790c" :question/math-academy-id "q-85897" :question/problem "In a town, blood tests are being carried out on all inhabitants to determine whether they have caught a virus. On average, $30%$ of the inhabitants test positive for the virus. What is the probability that the first positive test result will be made on the $3$rd test or later?" :question/worked-solution "A geometric random variable $X$ with probability of success $p$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=(1-p)^{x-1}p\n$$\n\nLet $X$ be the number of inhabitants checked until the first infected patient is found. Since the chance of a single patient being infected is $30%,$ the number of inhabitants checked until the first infected patient is found can be modeled as a geometric random variable with a probability of success\n\n$$\np=30%=\\frac{30}{100}=0.3.\n$$\n\nSo, $X∼\\text{Geom}(0.3).$ In this case, $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =(1-0.3)^{x-1}(0.3) \\\\  & =(0.7)^{x-1}(0.3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo compute $P(X\\ge 3),$ we will use the complement:\n\n$$\nP(X\\ge 3)=1-P(X<3)\n$$\n\nComputing the probability of the complement, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<3) & =P(X\\in \\{1,2\\}) \\\\  & =f(1)+f(2) \\\\  & =(0.7)^{1-1}(0.3)+(0.7)^{2-1}(0.3) \\\\  & =(0.3)+(0.7)(0.3) \\\\  & =[1+0.7](0.3) \\\\  & =0.51.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the probability of finding the first positive patient on the $3$rd test or later is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\ge 3) & =1-P(X<3) \\\\  & =1-0.51 \\\\  & =0.49.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186540087 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157317 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "42f47d95-9f20-5488-98c4-cb80278a7cf3" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Probability of a Geometric Random Variable on an Unbounded Interval"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09471886-d6ef-5fda-b2ee-571efe3d7fd3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.5472" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539497} {:answer/id #uuid "2c351f9d-e6dd-5545-9507-2a8c593f35e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.4980" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539561} {:answer/id #uuid "570a9d04-2464-5cc1-8a35-0e5260d61d27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.5120" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539628} {:answer/id #uuid "6bb6214c-874c-56eb-ac10-bd965a94ea7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.4795" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539658} {:answer/id #uuid "92ca3ed3-4800-5b9b-9a1e-c2593faee6b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.4096" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539722}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "92ca3ed3-4800-5b9b-9a1e-c2593faee6b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.4096" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539722} :answer-field/id #uuid "f5a73d02-83b1-5576-b29f-c152341639c1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540016}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "bc079e51-1277-52af-9686-51765572e614" :question/math-academy-id "q-85898" :question/problem "A professional soccer team participates in a championship. On average, the team has a $20%$ chance of losing each game. What is the probability that the team plays at least $4$ games without losing (i.e., the first loss occurs after the $4$th game)?" :question/worked-solution "A geometric random variable $X$ with probability of success $p$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=(1-p)^{x-1}p\n$$\n\nLet $X$ be the number of games played until they lose their first game. Since the chance of losing each game is $20%,$ the number of games played before the team loses can be modeled as a geometric random variable with a probability of success\n\n$$\np=20%=\\frac{20}{100}=0.2.\n$$\n\nSo, $X∼\\text{Geom}(0.2).$ In this case, $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =(1-0.2)^{x-1}(0.2) \\\\  & =(0.8)^{x-1}(0.2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo compute $P(X>4),$ we will use the complement:\n\n$$\nP(X>4)=1-P(X\\le 4)\n$$\n\nComputing the probability of the complement, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 4) & =P(X\\in \\{1,2,3,4\\}) \\\\  & =f(1)+f(2)+f(3)+f(4) \\\\  & =(0.8)^{1-1}(0.2)+(0.8)^{2-1}(0.2)+(0.8)^{3-1}(0.2)+(0.8)^{4-1}(0.2) \\\\  & =(0.2)+(0.8)(0.2)+(0.8)^{2}(0.2)+(0.8)^{3}(0.2) \\\\  & =[1+0.8+(0.8)^{2}+(0.8)^{3}](0.2) \\\\  & =0.5904.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the probability that the team will play at least $4$ games before their first loss\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>4) & =1-P(X\\le 4) \\\\  & =1-0.5904 \\\\  & =0.4096.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
